WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.938
One economy contains a firms-by-markets
array.

2
00:00:02.938 --> 00:00:08.114
Its independent market problems provide
work for the GPU, although the steps

3
00:00:08.114 --> 00:00:11.565
inside each problem still depend on
earlier steps.

4
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:15.391
Place several compatible economies in one
batch.

5
00:00:15.391 --> 00:00:17.998
The extra dimension identifies the
economy.

6
00:00:17.998 --> 00:00:22.342
Each keeps its own parameters, market
shares, and stopping state.

7
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:28.793
The batch exposes more independent work to
GPU thread blocks.

8
00:00:28.793 --> 00:00:31.459
Several economies can occupy the device

9
00:00:31.459 --> 00:00:35.014
together, instead of submitting each
complete economy separately.

10
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:40.479
Keep working arrays on the device and
reuse compatible operations.

11
00:00:40.479 --> 00:00:43.368
This can reduce repeated setup and
transfers.

12
00:00:43.368 --> 00:00:46.258
Finished economies can leave the active
batch.

13
00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:51.232
A larger batch also needs more memory.

14
00:00:51.232 --> 00:00:54.938
Occupancy, temporary arrays and uneven
convergence affect the result.

15
00:00:54.938 --> 00:00:56.585
Measure the complete solve;

16
00:00:56.585 --> 00:00:59.467
batch size alone does not guarantee speed.
